  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Before step 3: deployment is separate",
      "items": [
        "Human deployment credentials create roles through Terraform/CloudFormation after approval. They are never supplied to Hermes.",
        "STS does not create a role or modify trust. It evaluates existing authorization and returns temporary credentials or AccessDenied."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "No credential escalation chain",
      "items": [
        "Every target assumption starts from the host identity, not the local audit identity. Reader roles explicitly deny onward AssumeRole.",
        "The desk keeps credentials in its own process. Hermes receives the result, not access keys or session tokens."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What happens after a proposed fix",
      "items": [
        "A human-approved triage decision updates CE records only. IaC proposals use an isolated validator.",
        "The operator deploys infrastructure through their existing delivery process; chat approval cannot grant IAM access."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Scope",
      "items": [
        "This illustrates the containerized AWS deployment and explicitly provisioned cross-account roles. The diagram itself does not deploy IAM permissions.",
        "Managed MCP can transport an investigation request; the desk still owns guarded credentials. Collection uses the direct SDK."
      ]
    }
  ]
